relative log sensitivity with 0 set at the lower rule and 1.0 at the upper rule (absolute offset not printed). Sensitivity is the reciprocal of the exposure (J/cm2) required to produce a specified density, which the sheet gives as 1.0 above D-min. Three layers only. b runs about 400-507 nm, g about 461-598 nm, r about 565-674 nm; each curve ends in near-vertical drops, so the last few nm are approximated on the 5 nm grid.","Spectral dye density plot has only 'mid' (Mid-scale Density: typical densities for a mid-scale neutral subject) and 'min' (Minimum Density), no separate c/m/y dyes; the curves run about 400-720 nm.","Process: the plots say CN-16 (Fuji's name); page 3 says Vista films are process-compatible and are developed in AP 70 / CN-16 / C-41. Film speed ISO 200/24 deg daylight (tungsten 3200 K: ISO 50 with Wratten 80A or LBB-12). The sheet says 'when printed on AgfaPhoto papers' without naming a paper."],"print":"kodak-endura-premier"}